    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's examine the conversation line by line and explore the French expressions.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "hicham",
      "t": "Qu'est-ce que tu fais, là?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you doing here?' Hicham storms into Mathias's office demanding answers. The inverted question expresses agitated disbelief.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lea",
      "t": "Mais calme-toi, s'il te plaît.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Calm down, please.' Mathias tries to soothe his furious partner. The imperative 'calm' urges composure.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "hicham",
      "t": "C'est quoi ce terrible bordel?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What kind of terrible mess is this?' Hicham demands an explanation of the chaos. The colloquial French noun 'mess' describes complete disarray.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "hicham",
      "t": "Andréa veut partir avec Gabriel?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Andrea wants to leave with Gabriel?' Hicham confirms the identities of the defecting agents. The verb 'to leave' means to leave or depart.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "hicham",
      "t": "Monter une autre agence concurrente?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Start another competing agency?' Hicham cannot believe they plan to set up a rival company. The verb 'set up' here means to found or set up.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "hicham",
      "t": "Ce n'est pas possible!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This cannot be possible!' Hicham reacts with sheer disbelief to the revelation. The adjective 'possible' describes potential reality.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "hicham",
      "t": "Je suis complètement écœuré aujourd'hui.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am completely disgusted today.' Hicham confesses his deep personal revulsion at their disloyalty. The adjective 'ecoeure' expresses profound disgust.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lea",
      "t": "Je te comprends parfaitement, Hicham.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I understand you perfectly, Hicham.' Mathias adopts a sympathetic tone to gain his confidence. The adverb 'perfectly' means thoroughly or completely.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lea",
      "t": "Ma proposition tient toujours, sache-le.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My offer still stands, know that.' Mathias brings back his buyout proposal. The verbal idiom 'holds' means to remain valid.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "hicham",
      "t": "Tu veux acheter mes parts?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You want to buy out my shares?' Hicham clarifies Mathias's intentions. The noun 'parts' denotes company ownership shares.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lea",
      "t": "Je veux te libérer enfin.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I want to free you at last.' Mathias frames the buyout as liberating Hicham from unwanted stress. The verb 'to free' means to release or free.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lea",
      "t": "Tes associés te trahissent lâchement.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Your partners betray you cowardly.' Mathias drives a wedge between Hicham and his associates. The adverb 'cowardly' means cowardly or deceitfully.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "hicham",
      "t": "Et avec toi, ce sera différent?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And with you, it will be different?' Hicham questions whether Mathias is truly trustworthy. The future tense 'it' looks ahead to prospective ownership.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lea",
      "t": "ASK, c'est mon agence.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'ASK is my agency.' Mathias asserts his deep emotional and historical bond to ASK. The possessive determiner 'my' claims rightful leadership. Now let's listen to the complete discussion once more to reinforce the vocabulary.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
